  "description": "This simple corn casserole is one of the most comforting dishes I know. Cornmeal gives this baked custard an unusual heartiness, but with plenty of milk and eggs, it’s not bready at all.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: white cornmeal → yellow cornmeal\n\nNotes: This casserole can be prepared in a 30-cm cast iron skillet, but will cook faster on the stove and in the oven, so use the visual cues as your guide. If you don’t have a cast iron skillet, prepare the casserole in a large stainless steel skillet, then transfer to a 7- by 28-cm glass or ceramic dish to bake.",
